schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: "Walmart mango traceback dropped from ~7 days to 2.2 seconds on Hyperledger Fabric"
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    "In a pilot tracing mangoes, finding a fruit's origin dropped from about
    seven days to 2.2 seconds" using Hyperledger Fabric.
  evidence: >-
    Attributed to the LF Decentralized Trust Walmart case study, linked in
    the article's references.
  source_lineage: "src/content/docs/what-is-blockchain.md — LF Decentralized Trust: Walmart case study (https://www.lfdecentralizedtrust.org/case-studies/walmart-case-study)"
  interpretation: >-
    Used as the enterprise-scale comparison point for how a shared,
    checkable record turns a contamination-scare investigation from days of
    guesswork into a same-minute answer.
  uncertainty: >-
    Pilot-result figures reported by the platform steward's own case study;
    not independently re-verified against Walmart's own disclosures here.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
